  "lineage": "Music of the Pala'wan of the southern Palawan highlands: the basal ensemble of hanging bossed gongs with a drum, played at rice-wine feasts and rituals; the two-string kusyapi boat lute, played solo; and the tultul epic, chanted through the night by a bard. The kutiyapi card stands in for the kusyapi, and the gong card (bossed) for the basal gongs.",
